## Latest source snapshot and readiness caution

**Material receipt conflict:** the captured M1 branch's `docs/product/README.md` still identifies the October 13 PRD, while its populated native task register and `source-baseline.json` allocate October 15 V10. The separate maintained design checkout's product navigation identifies V10. These pointers are not reconciled by choosing whichever file was read last. V10 is the implementation register's captured input; the branch's stale navigation must be resolved through the owning records before a product-obligation change. The 270,791-byte implementation V10 snapshot includes a terminal LF difference from the 270,790-byte canonical source; record exact bytes separately from meaning.

The latest detached checkout at `AI4Research-Development/jiuwenswarm-m1-review-d3d7f56` is captured in [Current Baseline](../Resources/Current%20Baseline.md). It updates the native [M1 task register](../../AI4Research-Development/jiuwenswarm-m1-review-d3d7f56/docs/code/Missions/M1/TASKS.md) from the earlier `98bd9d9` checkout. The recorded 35-path delta changes web/authentication/deployment and M1-001/M1-006 records; the CC body, check-bundle, runner, and native-adapter files inspected in the earlier review are byte/source unchanged in that comparison. Do not combine old test counts or readiness statements with the new snapshot as if they were produced against it. New task-register assertions describe required work and status; they are not equivalent to a run, test, or acceptance result. The current TASKS register is populated (r45), but the receipt says integrated candidate NOT_BUILT and final system evidence NOT_RUN. Source presence and test sources do not establish acceptance or a CC accuracy gain.

## Decision rule for amendments

An amendment draft is not accepted architecture. Each proposed coder-facing change must point to the maintained PRD clause, current design decision/contract, concrete observed gap, and native task identity. If it changes an obligation or authority boundary, it needs an explicit authorized product decision and an update in the owning design/PRD process. If it only clarifies an implementation contract, preserve existing acceptance identities and request source-backed acceptance evidence. Do not silently carry personal directives, old workshop rules, or conditional planning assumptions into code instructions.

Coverage is bounded. The review batch documents the selected source files and hashes; it does not claim exhaustive PRD clause verification, complete approval-chain reconstruction, or a fresh test/build of the latest code.

## Native responsibility map

The populated [captured task register](../../AI4Research-Development/jiuwenswarm-m1-review-d3d7f56/docs/code/Missions/M1/TASKS.md) allocates the following owners. These are implementation responsibilities, not proof of AC completion. Read each owner's `spec.md` for actual AC identities and `tasks.md` for evidence; do not invent replacements from this notebook.

| Native owner | Responsibility | Code/evidence route |
|---|---|---|
| M1-001 | Native composition, runtime/dependency qualification and shared ports | Native adapter/bridge; M1-001 tasks |
| M1-002 | Store, library, binding, runner, checks/gates and evidence custody | Shared Enforcement reference; M1-002 tasks |
| M1-003 | Uploaded inputs through Intent and Requirements to accepted Brief | Compiler references; M1-003 tasks |
| M1-004 | Search through Delivery, environment/POC/scientific results | Research-stage references; M1-004 tasks |
| M1-005 | Planner proposals and protected planned execution | Planner reference; M1-005 tasks |
| M1-006 | Control API, CLI/web/TUI, installation, account/input inspection | Captured 35-file delta and M1-006 tasks |
| M1-007 | Separate router selection and bounded IPC; bridge retains dispatch | Routing agreement and M1-007 tasks |
| M1-008 | Offline candidate evolution, independent referee and manual promotion | Current design D21/D46 and M1-008 tasks |
| M1-QA | Independent tooling cases, protected scoring and evidence adapters | QA tasks; separate from product release gate |
| M1-SYSTEM | Same-candidate integrated journeys and acceptance evidence | System tasks; current final evidence NOT_RUN |

